<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Sepap to pay no 1996 div.</title>
<headline>Czech Sepap to pay no 1996 div.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech paper maker Sepap a.s. will pay no dividend for 1996, unchanged from 1995, after the firm posted a 316.8 million crown 1996 net loss and incurred high investment costs.</p>
<p>Sepap Director Tomas Sabatka told a news conference that Sepap should return to profitability in 1997, with an expected net profit of some 200-300 million crowns.</p>
</text>
